{"name":"door_leak_by_type","saveFile":"minimal_colony.rws","description":"Three identical 7x7 roofed rooms, one noon shot each, differing only in door type: plain wood Door (baseline 160 HP, blockLight true), Odyssey's AncientBlastDoor (6000 HP, blockLight true -- should leak far less than the baseline), and Workshop 3262718980's RB_GlassAutodoor (blockLight false -- should leak fully, same as no occlusion at all). Roofed with RoofConstructed (isThickRoof false), deliberately NOT RoofRockThick: a thick roof buries the wall ring itself in BlocksSky's thickRoof exception (issue #129), which would make the wall tiles unreadable in the screenshot alongside the door differentiation this scenario exists to show. Runs under the Realistic preset (MinIndoorBrightness=0) so Cinematic's shared 0.50 brightness floor doesn't clamp every occlusion above it to the same alpha, masking the per-door differentiation this scenario exists to show. Verifies IndoorOcclusionMath.DoorSkyLeakFor's per-door scaling actually reaches the rendered frame, not just the offline formula. Requires ReBuild.COTR.DoorsAndCorners (and its hard dependency OskarPotocki.VanillaFactionsExpanded.Core) in the mod list for the glass door; AncientBlastDoor ships with the Odyssey DLC.","steps":[
